    "eco.bio_title": "Why biodegradable ingredients matter",
    "eco.breakdown": "Some ingredients in cleaning products can break down through natural processes. Biodegradability may reduce the risk of chemicals persisting in the environment.",
    "eco.assessment": "Biodegradability alone does not guarantee that a product is completely safe. Consider its environmental and safety characteristics together when making a choice.",
    "eco.energy_title": "Reducing water and energy use",
    "eco.operations": "Water and energy used in professional cleaning directly affect operating costs. Well-chosen products, efficient procedures and modern dosing systems help businesses make better use of resources.",
    "eco.temperature": "For example, detergents designed to work at low temperatures can save energy under suitable conditions. When correctly dosed, concentrated products can also reduce packaging and transport needs.",
    "eco.pack_title": "Sustainable packaging and waste management",
    "eco.packaging": "Reducing packaging waste is an important sustainability goal in the cleaning sector. Recyclable packaging, refill systems and concentrated products are among the available solutions.",
    "eco.sorting": "Businesses should take care to sort used packaging correctly and dispose of it in line with local waste management rules.",
    "eco.strategy": "A sustainable hygiene strategy for businesses",
    "eco.practice": "Sustainable hygiene goes beyond buying products with environmental benefits. It includes educating staff, improving cleaning procedures, tracking resource use and making ongoing improvements.",
    "eco.reputation": "Restaurants, hotels, manufacturers and other organizations can improve operating efficiency and strengthen their reputations by adopting an environmentally responsible cleaning strategy.",
    "eco.end": "Eco-friendly cleaners and sustainable hygiene solutions play an important part in building a more responsible future. Choosing suitable products, using resources efficiently and reducing waste make it possible to maintain high hygiene standards while minimizing environmental harm.",
    "public.title": "Why hygiene standards matter in public spaces",
